
COMPUTER NETWORKS LABORATORY
Cisco Packet Tracer – Practical Setup Steps

BEFORE STARTING ANY QUESTION

1. Open Cisco Packet Tracer.
2. Place at least 2 routers and 3 switches.
3. Add PCs and servers according to the question.
4. Connect PCs to switches using Copper Straight-Through cables.
5. Connect switches to routers.
6. Give proper names to all devices.
7. Create separate IP networks for departments.
8. Assign IP addresses to router interfaces.
9. Configure VLANs wherever required.
10. Configure trunk ports wherever required.
11. Configure routing between different networks.
12. Configure DHCP wherever required.
13. Configure DNS, HTTP, FTP and Email services.
14. Test connectivity using ping.
15. Save the Packet Tracer file with your SIC number.

QUESTION 1: SMART UNIVERSITY CAMPUS NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Administration, CSE, ECE, Mechanical, Library, Examination and Hostel.
3. Add servers for DNS, Web, FTP and Email.
4. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect the switches with each other and connect the router to the main switch.
6. Create separate VLANs for all departments.
7. Create VLAN 10 for Admin, VLAN 20 for CSE, VLAN 30 for ECE, VLAN 40 for Mechanical, VLAN 50 for Library, VLAN 60 for Examination and VLAN 70 for Hostel.
8. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
9. Configure trunk ports between switches.
10. Configure router subinterfaces using encapsulation dot1Q.
11. Assign gateway IP addresses to all VLANs.
12. Connect both routers and configure their IP addresses.
13. Configure RIPv2 on both routers.
14. Configure DHCP pools and enable DNS, HTTP, FTP and Email services.
15. Test connectivity between departments and access all server services.

QUESTION 2: SMART HOSPITAL NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Reception, OPD, Emergency, Laboratory, Operation Theatre, Pharmacy, Accounts and Administration.
3. Add a server for DNS and the hospital web portal.
4. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect switches to each other and connect the router to the main switch.
6. Create separate VLANs for clinical, administrative and guest departments.
7. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
8. Configure trunk ports between switches.
9. Configure router subinterfaces for inter-VLAN communication.
10. Assign different gateway IP addresses to each VLAN.
11. Connect the second router and configure its IP address.
12. Configure static routing between both routers.
13. Configure DHCP pools for different departments.
14. Enable DNS and HTTP services on the hospital server.
15. Test connectivity and verify access to the hospital web portal.

QUESTION 3: MULTI-BRANCH BANKING NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Create one Head Office and four branches A, B, C and D.
3. Add PCs for every branch.
4. Add Database, ATM, DNS and Email servers at the Head Office.
5. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
6. Connect the branch networks to the routers using suitable WAN links.
7. Assign different IP networks to Head Office and all branches.
8. Configure IP addresses on router interfaces.
9. Assign gateway addresses to all branch networks.
10. Configure DHCP pools for branch PCs.
11. Configure static routes between the routers.
12. Enable DNS and Email services on the Head Office servers.
13. Enable FTP service for backup purposes.
14. Test connectivity between branch PCs and Head Office servers.
15. Verify routing tables and save the Packet Tracer file.

QUESTION 4: E-COMMERCE COMPANY NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Sales, Customer Support, Logistics, Finance and IT.
3. Add servers for Website, Database, Customer Portal, DNS and Email.
4. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
5. Create separate VLANs for all departments.
6. Create one additional VLAN for the Server Farm.
7. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
8. Configure trunk ports between switches.
9. Configure router subinterfaces for all VLANs.
10. Assign gateway IP addresses to each VLAN.
11. Connect the second router and configure routing.
12. Configure DHCP pools for all user departments.
13. Assign static IP addresses to all servers.
14. Enable HTTP, DNS, FTP and Email services and configure ACLs for access restrictions.
15. Test website access, DNS resolution, email communication and authorized FTP access.

QUESTION 5: SMART CITY COMMUNICATION NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add networks for Police Stations, Hospitals, Municipal Office, Schools and Fire Stations.
3. Add PCs for every location.
4. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect switches to the routers.
6. Assign different IP networks to all locations.
7. Configure IP addresses on router interfaces.
8. Configure DHCP pools for local networks.
9. Enable RIPv2 on both routers.
10. Advertise all connected networks using network commands.
11. Add a central monitoring server.
12. Add a public information web server and enable HTTP service.
13. Configure DNS and add a domain name for the website.
14. Test connectivity between different city networks and disconnect one redundant link to check alternate connectivity.
15. Save the topology and verify routing tables.

QUESTION 6: AIRPORT NETWORKING SYSTEM

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Check-In, Security, Air Traffic Control, Baggage Handling and Administration.
3. Add Flight Information and DNS servers.
4. Connect all PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect switches with each other and connect the router to the main switch.
6. Create separate VLANs for all operational departments.
7. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
8. Configure trunk ports between switches.
9. Configure router subinterfaces using dot1Q encapsulation.
10. Assign different gateway IP addresses to each VLAN.
11. Connect the second router and configure its IP address.
12. Configure static routing or RIP as required.
13. Configure DHCP pools for all VLANs.
14. Enable DNS and HTTP services on the servers.
15. Test connectivity and open the Flight Information Portal from different PCs.

QUESTION 7: CORPORATE ENTERPRISE NETWORK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Divide the network into three floors.
3. Add PCs for HR and Administration on Floor 1.
4. Add PCs for Finance and Sales on Floor 2.
5. Add PCs for IT Department on Floor 3.
6. Add a server for DNS and the internal web portal.
7. Connect each floor's PCs to its respective switch.
8. Create separate VLANs for HR, Administration, Finance, Sales and IT.
9. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
10. Configure trunk ports between floor switches.
11. Configure router-on-a-stick for inter-VLAN routing.
12. Assign gateway IP addresses to all VLANs.
13. Configure DHCP pools for all departments.
14. Enable DNS and HTTP services and configure NAT on the edge router if supported.
15. Test communication within VLANs and between departments.

QUESTION 8: SMART MANUFACTURING PLANT

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Production, Warehouse, Quality Control, HR and Finance.
3. Add Inventory Server and Employee Management Portal server.
4. Connect PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect switches to each other and connect the routers.
6. Create separate VLANs for all departments.
7. Create an additional VLAN for the Server segment.
8. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
9. Configure trunk ports between switches.
10. Configure router subinterfaces for inter-VLAN routing.
11. Assign gateway IP addresses to each VLAN.
12. Configure DHCP pools for different departments.
13. Assign static IP addresses to servers and enable DNS and HTTP services.
14. Configure ACLs to allow only authorized departments to access designated servers.
15. Test authorized and unauthorized access and save the Packet Tracer file.

QUESTION 9: ISP NETWORK INFRASTRUCTURE

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Create one ISP Core Network and three Customer Networks.
3. Add PCs for all three customer networks.
4. Connect customer PCs to their respective switches.
5. Connect switches to the distribution and core routers.
6. Assign different IP subnets to all customer networks.
7. Configure IP addresses on router interfaces.
8. Configure DHCP pools for customer networks.
9. Configure OSPF or another suitable routing protocol.
10. Advertise all connected networks using appropriate network commands.
11. Configure NAT/PAT on the edge router if supported.
12. Add a DNS server and configure DNS services.
13. Add an external server to simulate an Internet service.
14. Test connectivity between customer networks and the external server.
15. Verify routing tables and save the topology.

QUESTION 10: CYBER SECURITY OPERATIONS CENTER (SOC)

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Add PCs for Security Analysts, Incident Response, Threat Intelligence and Management.
3. Add servers for SIEM, DNS, Threat Database and Dashboard.
4. Connect PCs and servers to their respective switches.
5. Create separate VLANs for all four teams.
6. Create one additional VLAN for the Server segment.
7. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
8. Configure trunk ports between switches.
9. Configure router subinterfaces for inter-VLAN routing.
10. Assign gateway IP addresses to all VLANs.
11. Connect the second router and configure routing.
12. Configure DHCP pools for team networks.
13. Enable DNS and HTTP services on the servers.
14. Configure ACLs to restrict access to security databases and allow only Management to access designated reports.
15. Test authorized and unauthorized access and save the configuration.

QUESTION 11: SMART DIGITAL UNIVERSITY AND RESEARCH PARK

1. Open Packet Tracer and place 2 routers and 3 switches.
2. Create four zones: Academic, Administrative, Residential and Research.
3. Add PCs for Engineering, MBA, MCA and Library.
4. Add PCs for Administration, Accounts and Examination Cell.
5. Add PCs for Boys Hostel and Girls Hostel.
6. Add PCs for AI Lab, IoT Lab and Cyber Security Lab.
7. Add five servers for DNS, DHCP, Web, FTP and Email services.
8. Create at least 10 VLANs with different VLAN IDs and IP subnets.
9. Assign switch ports to their respective VLANs.
10. Configure trunk ports between switches.
11. Configure inter-VLAN routing using router-on-a-stick or a multilayer switch.
12. Assign gateway IP addresses to all VLANs.
13. Configure routing between both routers.
14. Configure DHCP, DNS, HTTP, FTP and Email services on the data-centre servers.
15. Test connectivity, server access, file transfer and email communication.

USEFUL CISCO COMMANDS

Basic Configuration:
enable
configure terminal
hostname R1
exit
end
copy running-config startup-config

Interface Configuration:
interface gigabitEthernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

VLAN Configuration:
vlan 10
name ADMIN
exit

Access Port Configuration:
interface fastEthernet 0/1
switchport mode access
switchport access vlan 10
exit

Trunk Port Configuration:
interface fastEthernet 0/24
switchport mode trunk
no shutdown
exit

Router-on-a-Stick:
interface gigabitEthernet 0/0.10
encapsulation dot1Q 10
ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
exit

DHCP Configuration:
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.10.1 192.168.10.10
ip dhcp pool ADMIN
network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
default-router 192.168.10.1
dns-server 192.168.10.10
exit

RIP Configuration:
router rip
version 2
no auto-summary
network 192.168.1.0
exit

Static Routing:
ip route 192.168.2.0 255.255.255.0 192.168.1.2

Useful Verification Commands:
show vlan brief
show interfaces trunk
show ip interface brief
show ip route
show ip protocols
show ip dhcp binding
show running-config

Connectivity Test:
ping 192.168.1.1
traceroute 192.168.2.1

FINAL SUBMISSION CHECKLIST

1. Save the Packet Tracer file using your SIC number.
2. Include at least 2 routers and 3 switches.
3. Give proper names to all devices and networks.
4. Prepare an IP addressing table.
5. Prepare a VLAN table wherever VLANs are used.
6. Take a screenshot of the complete network topology.
7. Take screenshots of VLAN and trunk configurations.
8. Take screenshots of routing tables wherever routing is used.
9. Show successful connectivity using ping.
10. Include screenshots of DHCP, DNS, HTTP, FTP and Email tests wherever required.
